From 51f2e38b186d9ff3ebd503bc66aed238bf20ae5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Buergel <SCBuergel@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:03:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(pix): send the payment relayer's traffic through its
 own session

The exit holds a session's return traffic back once the session's free allowance
(10,000 packets, about 13 MB) is used up and it has not seen the deposit. The
deposit goes to the Curvy relayer through the VPN tunnel, so the relayer's answers
are held back with everything else and the deposit can no longer be made. The
connection then stays dead until the exit's deposit timeout (3 minutes).

When connecting, open one more unpaid session through the exit to the relayer and
point the payment pool's relayer route (edgli RelayerRoute) at its listener. The
route opens the first connection right away, in parallel with the main session.
Closed again on disconnect. If the session cannot be opened the client connects as
before.

The exit has to allow the relayer as a session target (api.curvy.box:443).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DhJoLT7WGUfYpeAy7hDvmZ
