From c768ccf1b96ed441cb885429ca426de20b2d2734 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Buergel <SCBuergel@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:03:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(pix): hold the tunnel until the first payment is
 confirmed

With the relayer on its own session the first deposit no longer depends on the
tunnel. Wait for it before attaching the tunnel, so the user's traffic never runs on
the exit's free allowance and never stops while the deposit is under way. The wait
moves from after "connected" to before it.

The client cannot observe the exit's confirmation. After its own pool reports the
deposit as made it waits a fixed 22 s (3 block confirmations plus the pool operator's
commit; measured 18.6 to 26.0 s from the relayer's acceptance). After 150 s without a
deposit it drops the side-car route and connects without the hold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DhJoLT7WGUfYpeAy7hDvmZ
